comments/4325569288","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118988#issuecomment-4325569288","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118988","id":4325569288,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAdLzCA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-27T08:56:21Z","updated_at":"2026-04-27T08:56:21Z","body":"The CI workload won't be fixed if we add more runs, adding 6 new workflows means much higher congestion\r\n\r\nAlso CI should run for all PRs as it's not trivial to know if something needs to be confirmed on specific targets or not, even if it doesn't touch area specific code","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4325569288/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4325571697","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118988#issuecomment-4325571697","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118988","id":4325571697,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAdL8cQ","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-27T08:56:43Z","updated_at":"2026-04-27T08:59:03Z","body":"Indeed, I agree in general that having some CI would be good to validate that these platforms don't regress. But our CI budget is already huge and this would increase it too much. Those platforms are very niche (we're talking maybe a few hundred potential users?) and while it matters to me that they're supported if we can, we need to find a reasonable tradeoff.\r\n\r\nI think for this, and other niche platforms / configurations (`double` precision builds, `deprecated=no`, etc. and a various other items not tested currently by the build matrix), we should have a separate workflow that's not triggered on all PRs / pushes, but either manually or on a cron job (e.g. once per week). So we can confirm that we're still building for all platforms we aim to keep working, without adding too much delay and waste resources with 50-100 daily CI workflows.\r\n\r\n> What about making it only runable when it has a *bsd label?\r\nAs not a lot of pr get made fod *bsd typd systems, that seems to me like a good compromise(at least until the CI workload is fixed)\r\n\r\nThat could be done, but it wouldn't help much. *BSD builds would typically be broken not by PRs explicitly targeting those platforms, but PRs modifying other stuff like thirdparty code, `core/{io,os}`, `drivers/unix`, `platform/linuxbsd`, etc. If we include everything that can affect BSD builds, then we'd basically end up still running it most of the time.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4325571697/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4325645362","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118988#issuecomment-4325645362","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118988","id":4325645362,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAdQcMg","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-27T09:07:18Z","updated_at":"2026-04-27T09:07:18Z","body":"> Also I've disabled AccessKit because builds for the BSDs are not included in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-accesskit-c-static .\r\n\r\nIt would make sense to add builders for BSDs to it. Unlike the main repo, it should not be an issue since it only runs when new releases are made (but we might need to reorganize how artifacts are packed to avoid downloading unneeded libs for all platforms).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4325645362/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4325795756","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118988#issuecomment-4325795756","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118988","id":4325795756,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAdZnrA","user":{"login":"DeanLemans","id":111811264,"node_id":"U_kgDOBqoawA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111811264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans","html_url":"https://github.com/DeanLemans","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeanLemans/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-27T09:30:17Z","updated_at":"2026-04-27T09:31:18Z","body":"> Indeed, I agree in general that having some CI would be good to validate that these platforms don't regress. But our CI budget is already huge and this would increase it too much. Those platforms are very niche (we're talking maybe a few hundred potential users?) and while it matters to me that they're supported if we can, we need to find a reasonable tradeoff.\r\n> \r\n> I think for this, and other niche platforms / configurations (`double` precision builds, `deprecated=no`, etc. and a various other items not tested currently by the build matrix), we should have a separate workflow that's not triggered on all PRs / pushes, but either manually or on a cron job (e.g. once per week). So we can confirm that we're still building for all platforms we aim to keep working, without adding too much delay and waste resources with 50-100 daily CI workflows.\r\n> \r\n> > What about making it only runable when it has a *bsd label?\r\n> > As not a lot of pr get made fod *bsd typd systems, that seems to me like a good compromise(at least until the CI workload is fixed)\r\n> \r\n> That could be done, but it wouldn't help much. *BSD builds would typically be broken not by PRs explicitly targeting those platforms, but PRs modifying other stuff like thirdparty code, `core/{io,os}`, `drivers/unix`, `platform/linuxbsd`, etc. If we include everything that can affect BSD builds, then we'd basically end up still running it most of the time.\r\n\r\nA option would be to use third party github actions providers in order to lessen CI cost:\r\n\r\n- [Blacksmith](https://www.blacksmith.sh/)\r\n- [WarpBuild](https://www.warpbuild.com/)\r\n- [BuildJet](https://buildjet.com/for-github-actions)\r\n- [RunsOn](https://runs-on.com/)\r\n- [Namespace](https://namespace.so/)\r\n- [Cirun](https://cirun.io/)\r\n- [RunMyJob](https://runmyjob.io/)\r\n- [Depot](https://depot.dev/)\r\n\r\nA long(er) term solution would be to build our own build/CI farm, where people can contribute their own PC power to the project/CI\r\n\r\n- [OpenMandriva docker-builder](https://github.com/OpenMandrivaSoftware/docker-builder)\r\n- [Buildfarm (distributed build system)](https://github.com/buildfarm/buildfarm)\r\n- [Buildkite Agent Documentation](https://buildkite.com/docs/agent)\r\n- [Jenkins](https://www.jenkins.io/)\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4325795756/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4325823708","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118988#issuecomment-4325823708","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118988","id":4325823708,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAdbU3A","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-27T09:34:56Z","updated_at":"2026-04-27T09:35:46Z","body":"\"Cost\" in this case is to be understood as \"time\" and \"power consumption\". We don't actually pay for GitHub Actions minutes as an open source project, this is sponsored by GitHub.\r\n\r\nAnd well potential _future_ cost if we were to move off GitHub and had to pay for CI (in which case we'd have to reduce the build matrix even further than what we have now).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4325823708/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4325913695","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118988#issuecomment-4325913695","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118988","id":4325913695,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAdg0Xw","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/user